      <tei:div facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n274.jpg">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:areshet_sefatenu/opening"/>May the utterance of our lips be pleasing before Thee, O lofty and exalted God, who understands and listens, pays heed and hearkens to the sound of  <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:areshet_sefatenu/conclusion"/><tei:choice><j:option corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:condition:prayer:areshet_sefatenu/conclusion/en/first_printing"> our Teruah. Mayest Thou accept with compassion and favour the order of our praises of Thy Kingdom.</j:option><j:option corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:condition:prayer:areshet_sefatenu/conclusion/en/zikhronot_printing"> our Tekiah. Mayest Thou accept with compassion and favour the order of our verses of remembrance.</j:option></tei:choice> <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
